Odin mal implementation (work in progress).

Requires libedit (for readline-compatible input/history).

Ubuntu install:
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y libedit-dev

Bindings are laid out in a vendor-style package:
- vendor/editline/bindgen.sjson
- vendor/editline/editline__foreign.odin
- vendor/editline/input/editline_bindings.h
- vendor/editline/editline_bindings.odin (generated)
- vendor/editline/editline.odin (wrapper API)

Install/build odin-c-bindgen (user-local, no sudo):
  git clone https://github.com/karl-zylinski/odin-c-bindgen /tmp/odin-c-bindgen
  odin build /tmp/odin-c-bindgen/src -out:/tmp/odin-c-bindgen/bindgen.bin
  install -d ~/.local/bin
  install -m 0755 /tmp/odin-c-bindgen/bindgen.bin ~/.local/bin/bindgen

If your Odin version cannot build odin-c-bindgen, use a prebuilt binary path instead:
  make -C impls/odin BINDGEN=/path/to/bindgen.bin bindings

Build step0:
  make

Run REPL for step0:
  STEP=step0_repl ./run

Run tests for step0 from repo root:
  make "test^odin^step0"

Run step0 tests in Docker from repo root:
  make "docker-build^odin"
  make DOCKERIZE=1 "test^odin^step0"

Regenerate bindings (with odin-c-bindgen):
  make -C impls/odin bindings
  make -C impls/odin BINDGEN=/path/to/bindgen.bin bindings
